Functional Testing: Checks what the system does

* Verifies features against requirements
* Focuses on inputs → outputs
* Ensures the application works correctly
Types of functional testings are:
Unit Testing
Integration Testing
System Testing
Acceptance Testing (UAT - User Acceptance Testing)

Non-Functional Testing: Checks how the system performs
* Focuses on performance, usability, reliability, security
* Ensures system works well under different conditions

Types of non-functional testings are:
Performance Testing (load, stress)
Security Testing
Usability Testing
Compatibility Testing

We choose non-functional testing when performance, scalability, security, or user experience is critical, such as in high-traffic applications like e-commerce or banking systems.
